AB  - Abstract: Objective To investigate the effects of early family nursing intervention on the quality of life of patients with Alzheimer's disease(AD)at earl y and middle stage.Methods Fifty-two patients diagnosed with early or mid-term AD were equally randomized into the observational group and the contro I group.The control group received routine discharged guidance without any post-discharge nursing intervention.Besides routine guidance,the patients a nd caregivers of the observational group received family nursing intervention,such as education and nursing skills training of treatment compliance on A D,psychological nursing,home safety nursing,rehabilitation training.Before and after the intervention,mini mental state examination(MMSE),activities of d aily living(ADL)and health survey questionnaire(SF-36)were employed to evaluate the quality of life of patients in the two groups.Results After interventio n,the ADL score of the observational group and the composite score of SF-36 were 15.86±3.81 and 578.3±142.4 respectively,which were both significant ly higher than that of the control group(P<0.05).The MMSE score of the observational group was 16.12±2.84,which was significantly different from that of the control group(P<0.01);Significant differences were observed on the eight domains somatic health,social function,somatic role function,somatic pain,p sychological health emotional role function,the general health and energy between the observational group and the control group(P<0.05 or P<0.01).Con clusion Family nursing intervention can improve the self-care ability,quality of life and psychological adaptation ability and alleviate their illness advances of the patients with early or mid-term AD.
